[
  {
    "text": "A single Nvidia accelerator can sell for",
    "start": 0.311,
    "end": 2.953,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "$30,000 or more. It is one of",
    "start": 3.114,
    "end": 5.075,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "the most complex pieces of engineering",
    "start": 5.095,
    "end": 7.057,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "ever mass produced. Yet without a small",
    "start": 7.157,
    "end": 9.519,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "stack of memory built by one company",
    "start": 9.579,
    "end": 11.381,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "in South Korea, that accelerator is a",
    "start": 11.441,
    "end": 13.643,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "very expensive piece of sand. The memory",
    "start": 13.683,
    "end": 16.285,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "is high bandwidth memory. The company is",
    "start": 16.425,
    "end": 18.807,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix. Why Nvidia cannot simply buy",
    "start": 19.007,
    "end": 21.87,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "it somewhere else is a story about",
    "start": 21.91,
    "end": 23.911,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "physics, packaging, and a quiet chokehold.",
    "start": 23.991,
    "end": 26.754,
    "scene": "scene_01"
  },
  {
    "text": "The numbers are hard to ignore. NVIDIA",
    "start": 27.175,
    "end": 29.416,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "became one of the most valuable companies",
    "start": 29.456,
    "end": 31.437,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "by selling the shovels of the artificial",
    "start": 31.757,
    "end": 33.478,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "intelligence boom. Every data center GPU",
    "start": 33.518,
    "end": 36.339,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "needs high bandwidth memory, and the",
    "start": 36.379,
    "end": 38.22,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "supply is not elastic. SK Hynix says",
    "start": 38.26,
    "end": 41.161,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "its capacity sold out well before the",
    "start": 41.221,
    "end": 43.182,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "year began and warns shortages could",
    "start": 43.202,
    "end": 45.462,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "persist to the end of the decade.",
    "start": 45.502,
    "end": 47.043,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "When the bottleneck is measured in months",
    "start": 47.543,
    "end": 49.404,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "of factory time, memory stops being a",
    "start": 49.444,
    "end": 51.905,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "component. It becomes the schedule.",
    "start": 51.945,
    "end": 54.126,
    "scene": "scene_02"
  },
  {
    "text": "Computer architects have a name for the",
    "start": 54.567,
    "end": 56.268,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "gap between how fast a processor",
    "start": 56.308,
    "end": 58.129,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "calculates and how fast memory can feed",
    "start": 58.189,
    "end": 60.611,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "it. They call it the memory wall.",
    "start": 60.631,
    "end": 62.472,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "For decades, caches and profetching hid",
    "start": 62.912,
    "end": 65.294,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "that gap in general computing. Artificial",
    "start": 65.334,
    "end": 67.896,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "intelligence broke the illusion. A modern",
    "start": 67.936,
    "end": 70.497,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "model does not read data once. It",
    "start": 70.557,
    "end": 72.819,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "streams billions of parameters through the",
    "start": 72.839,
    "end": 74.86,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "chip for every token, and the arithmetic",
    "start": 74.92,
    "end": 77.362,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "units spend much of their time waiting",
    "start": 77.482,
    "end": 79.503,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "for the next number to arrive.",
    "start": 79.563,
    "end": 80.864,
    "scene": "scene_03"
  },
  {
    "text": "To understand why high bandwidth memory",
    "start": 81.305,
    "end": 83.207,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "exists, start with the graphics card you",
    "start": 83.287,
    "end": 85.449,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "already know. A gaming GPU sits on",
    "start": 85.489,
    "end": 87.991,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "a circuit board next to a handful",
    "start": 88.031,
    "end": 89.672,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "of memory chips. Those chips are called",
    "start": 89.712,
    "end": 91.834,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "graphics double data rate memory or GDDR.",
    "start": 91.894,
    "end": 94.877,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "They are cheap, dense, and fast in",
    "start": 95.317,
    "end": 97.239,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "the way a highway is fast when",
    "start": 97.279,
    "end": 98.96,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "traffic is light. The problem is not",
    "start": 99.02,
    "end": 101.122,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "the chips themselves. The problem is the",
    "start": 101.182,
    "end": 103.564,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "road between them and the processor.",
    "start": 103.644,
    "end": 105.686,
    "scene": "scene_04"
  },
  {
    "text": "On a flagship graphics card, the memory",
    "start": 106.147,
    "end": 108.329,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "bus is wide by historical standards, 384",
    "start": 108.389,
    "end": 111.571,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "bits on one generation, 512 bits on",
    "start": 112.291,
    "end": 115.433,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "the next. Each bit is a copper",
    "start": 115.453,
    "end": 117.594,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "trace rooted across a printed circuit",
    "start": 117.634,
    "end": 119.556,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "board, and every trace must arrive at",
    "start": 119.616,
    "end": 121.837,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "the processor at the same time. At",
    "start": 121.857,
    "end": 124.199,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "multi-gigabit speeds, a few millimeters of",
    "start": 124.259,
    "end": 126.92,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "extra length is no longer a detail.",
    "start": 127.08,
    "end": 129.202,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "It is a timing error.",
    "start": 129.742,
    "end": 130.903,
    "scene": "scene_05"
  },
  {
    "text": "Those copper traces behave like",
    "start": 131.324,
    "end": 132.906,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "transmission lines. They have capacitance,",
    "start": 132.946,
    "end": 135.348,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "inductance, and resistance. High frequency",
    "start": 135.588,
    "end": 138.03,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "signals leak, reflect, and interfere with",
    "start": 138.07,
    "end": 139.932,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "their neighbors. The further a signal",
    "start": 139.952,
    "end": 141.773,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "travels, the more energy it loses and",
    "start": 141.813,
    "end": 143.855,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "the more it distorts. Engineers compensate",
    "start": 143.875,
    "end": 146.377,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "with better substrates, more layers, and",
    "start": 146.397,
    "end": 148.419,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "careful shielding. But every fixed cost's",
    "start": 148.459,
    "end": 150.701,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "money adds thickness and consumes power.",
    "start": 150.781,
    "end": 153.283,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "You can only push a signal across",
    "start": 153.763,
    "end": 155.265,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "a circuit board so far before the",
    "start": 155.305,
    "end": 157.026,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "physical cost stops making sense.",
    "start": 157.046,
    "end": 159.048,
    "scene": "scene_06"
  },
  {
    "text": "There is a second cost that matters",
    "start": 159.469,
    "end": 161.05,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "even more in a data center. Moving",
    "start": 161.17,
    "end": 163.23,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "a bit of data across a wire",
    "start": 163.25,
    "end": 164.67,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "takes energy. The longer the wire and",
    "start": 164.731,
    "end": 167.011,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "the faster the signal, the more energy",
    "start": 167.031,
    "end": 169.192,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "that bit consumes. On a graphics card,",
    "start": 169.232,
    "end": 171.792,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "that energy becomes heat, and heat becomes",
    "start": 172.113,
    "end": 174.553,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "a cooling problem. Multiply it by hundreds",
    "start": 174.593,
    "end": 177.234,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "of billions of bits per second, and",
    "start": 177.274,
    "end": 179.295,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "the power bill becomes a design",
    "start": 179.315,
    "end": 180.975,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "constraint. The industry calls this the",
    "start": 181.035,
    "end": 183.396,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "energy per bit.",
    "start": 183.516,
    "end": 184.396,
    "scene": "scene_07"
  },
  {
    "text": "The memory wall is not a metaphor.",
    "start": 184.817,
    "end": 186.537,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "It is a measurable ratio between compute",
    "start": 186.937,
    "end": 188.958,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "throughput and memory bandwidth. Over the",
    "start": 189.018,
    "end": 191.398,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "last two decades, floating point",
    "start": 191.438,
    "end": 193.319,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "performance grew far faster than the",
    "start": 193.359,
    "end": 195.099,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "bandwidth of ordinary memory. For a while,",
    "start": 195.139,
    "end": 197.499,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "caches absorbed most of the traffic.",
    "start": 197.819,
    "end": 199.66,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "Artificial intelligence workloads are",
    "start": 200.12,
    "end": 201.92,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "different. They are dominated by matrix",
    "start": 201.96,
    "end": 204.261,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "multiplication, and matrix multiplication",
    "start": 204.321,
    "end": 206.841,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "is hungry for data. An arithmetic unit",
    "start": 206.941,
    "end": 209.561,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "with no data is just a very",
    "start": 209.601,
    "end": 211.402,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "expensive heater.",
    "start": 211.462,
    "end": 212.342,
    "scene": "scene_08"
  },
  {
    "text": "Modern language models make the problem",
    "start": 212.823,
    "end": 214.684,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "worse in two directions. Training requires",
    "start": 214.724,
    "end": 217.286,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "enormous data sets and repeated passes",
    "start": 217.346,
    "end": 219.607,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "over the same weights. Inference requires",
    "start": 219.707,
    "end": 221.929,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "reading the entire model for every token,",
    "start": 221.989,
    "end": 223.93,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "plus a growing cache of intermediate state",
    "start": 224.29,
    "end": 226.231,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "called the key value cache. Both workloads",
    "start": 226.431,
    "end": 228.833,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "care about capacity as much as bandwidth.",
    "start": 228.893,
    "end": 231.014,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "A GPU with insufficient memory cannot hold",
    "start": 231.515,
    "end": 233.956,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "the model, and a GPU with insufficient",
    "start": 233.976,
    "end": 236.398,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "bandwidth cannot keep its cores busy. You",
    "start": 236.458,
    "end": 239.139,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "need both at once.",
    "start": 239.159,
    "end": 240.1,
    "scene": "scene_09"
  },
  {
    "text": "So why not simply bolt more GDDR",
    "start": 240.541,
    "end": 242.483,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "chips onto the board? The answer is",
    "start": 242.563,
    "end": 244.564,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "pin count, board area and power. Each",
    "start": 244.644,
    "end": 247.287,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "additional chip needs its own data lanes,",
    "start": 247.347,
    "end": 249.368,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "its own power delivery, and its own",
    "start": 249.688,
    "end": 251.61,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "share of the thermal budget. A processor",
    "start": 251.67,
    "end": 253.972,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "can only drive so many high-speed pins",
    "start": 254.012,
    "end": 256.274,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "before the package becomes impractical.",
    "start": 256.494,
    "end": 258.315,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "You can widen the bus, but the",
    "start": 258.756,
    "end": 260.377,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "traces get longer, and signal integrity",
    "start": 260.417,
    "end": 262.899,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "gets worse. The architecture runs into a",
    "start": 263.119,
    "end": 265.681,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "wall made of copper.",
    "start": 265.741,
    "end": 266.682,
    "scene": "scene_10"
  },
  {
    "text": "The solution was to stop treating memory",
    "start": 267.103,
    "end": 269.105,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "as something that lives across the board,",
    "start": 269.245,
    "end": 270.947,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "put it directly on top of the",
    "start": 271.347,
    "end": 272.708,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "processor package. Stack the memory dies",
    "start": 272.748,
    "end": 275.311,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "vertically and connect the stack to the",
    "start": 275.371,
    "end": 277.292,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "GPU through a silicon interposer. That",
    "start": 277.332,
    "end": 280.035,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "idea became high bandwidth memory. Instead",
    "start": 280.115,
    "end": 282.777,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "of a few hundred bits rooted across",
    "start": 282.797,
    "end": 284.439,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "centimeters of circuit board, you get a",
    "start": 284.479,
    "end": 286.541,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "thousand bits rooted across millimeters of",
    "start": 286.581,
    "end": 288.763,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "silicon. The distance collapses and with",
    "start": 288.823,
    "end": 291.725,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "it the energy cost.",
    "start": 291.825,
    "end": 293.247,
    "scene": "scene_11"
  },
  {
    "text": "Inside the stack, the dies are connected",
    "start": 293.708,
    "end": 295.728,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "by through silicon wires or TSVs. These",
    "start": 295.788,
    "end": 298.849,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "are microscopic holes drilled through each",
    "start": 298.889,
    "end": 300.789,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "memory die and filled with copper.",
    "start": 300.849,
    "end": 302.43,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "Thousands run vertically through the",
    "start": 302.89,
    "end": 304.27,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "stack, carrying power, data and control",
    "start": 304.31,
    "end": 306.75,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "signals. Building them is brutal. The dies",
    "start": 306.81,
    "end": 309.571,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "must be thin to a fraction of",
    "start": 309.611,
    "end": 310.871,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "a millimeter, aligned with micron",
    "start": 310.911,
    "end": 312.932,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "precision and bonded without cracking. One",
    "start": 312.992,
    "end": 315.972,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "bad wire can ruin an entire stack,",
    "start": 316.032,
    "end": 318.092,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "and a stack may hold 16 dies.",
    "start": 318.453,
    "end": 319.633,
    "scene": "scene_12"
  },
  {
    "text": "The stack then sits on a silicon",
    "start": 320.054,
    "end": 321.715,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "interposer, a piece of silicon that acts",
    "start": 321.735,
    "end": 324.116,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "like a miniature motherboard. It carries",
    "start": 324.156,
    "end": 326.356,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "thousands of fine traces between the GPU",
    "start": 326.436,
    "end": 328.757,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "and the memory stacks. This is called",
    "start": 328.797,
    "end": 330.858,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "2.5D packaging because the chip sits side",
    "start": 330.918,
    "end": 333.959,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "by side rather than truly on top",
    "start": 334.019,
    "end": 336.0,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "of one another. It is expensive,",
    "start": 336.04,
    "end": 338.081,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "difficult, and the only practical way to",
    "start": 338.321,
    "end": 340.462,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "deliver enough bandwidth to a modern",
    "start": 340.502,
    "end": 342.302,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "accelerator. The interposer, not the",
    "start": 342.342,
    "end": 344.843,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "transistor, became the bottleneck.",
    "start": 344.863,
    "end": 346.904,
    "scene": "scene_13"
  },
  {
    "text": "Highband with memory has evolved through",
    "start": 347.365,
    "end": 349.366,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "several generations. The first version",
    "start": 349.426,
    "end": 351.708,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "arrived in 2013. HBM2 doubled the stack",
    "start": 351.788,
    "end": 355.21,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "height and data rate. HBM2E added 12",
    "start": 355.25,
    "end": 358.092,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "high stacks, then came HBM3 with a",
    "start": 358.132,
    "end": 361.074,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "thousand bit interface that pushed one",
    "start": 361.134,
    "end": 362.795,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "stack past 800 gigabytes per second. Each",
    "start": 362.855,
    "end": 365.897,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "generation required thinner dies, more",
    "start": 365.937,
    "end": 368.298,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "wires, and better packaging. By HBM3E, the",
    "start": 368.358,
    "end": 372.421,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "stack had become a packaging problem.",
    "start": 372.461,
    "end": 374.202,
    "scene": "scene_14"
  },
  {
    "text": "HBM3E is the generation that powered",
    "start": 374.743,
    "end": 377.445,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "Nvidia's Blackwell accelerators. A 12 high",
    "start": 377.505,
    "end": 380.347,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "stack holds 36 gigabytes and delivers",
    "start": 380.367,
    "end": 382.928,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "about 1.2 terabytes per second. Depending",
    "start": 382.968,
    "end": 385.89,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "on the accelerator, Nvidia pairs 4, 6,",
    "start": 385.95,
    "end": 388.672,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "or 8 stacks around the GPU. Total",
    "start": 389.032,
    "end": 391.454,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "bandwidth reaches 8 terabytes per second",
    "start": 391.514,
    "end": 393.695,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "on a flagship part. That is roughly",
    "start": 393.775,
    "end": 395.736,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "10 times the fastest consumer graphics",
    "start": 395.816,
    "end": 398.038,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "card achieved in a package that still",
    "start": 398.098,
    "end": 400.579,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "fits on a server board.",
    "start": 400.619,
    "end": 401.78,
    "scene": "scene_15"
  },
  {
    "text": "Stacking that many dies creates three",
    "start": 402.221,
    "end": 404.043,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "problems at once. The first is thickness.",
    "start": 404.083,
    "end": 406.525,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "To keep the package within a fixed",
    "start": 406.965,
    "end": 408.346,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "height, each die must be thinned as",
    "start": 408.406,
    "end": 410.288,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "more layers are added. A 12-high stack",
    "start": 410.348,
    "end": 412.83,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "uses dies roughly 40% thinner than an",
    "start": 412.95,
    "end": 415.212,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "8-high stack. The second is warpage. Thin",
    "start": 415.252,
    "end": 418.315,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "silicon bends under heat and pressure. The",
    "start": 418.395,
    "end": 420.757,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "third is heat. Every die generates power,",
    "start": 420.797,
    "end": 423.559,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "and that heat must escape through the",
    "start": 423.919,
    "end": 425.501,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "same narrow path.",
    "start": 425.561,
    "end": 426.562,
    "scene": "scene_16"
  },
  {
    "text": "To hold the stack together, manufacturers",
    "start": 427.003,
    "end": 429.184,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "use a packaging process. The conventional",
    "start": 429.284,
    "end": 431.504,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "approach is called thermal compression",
    "start": 431.544,
    "end": 433.324,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "non-conductive film or TC-NCF. A film of",
    "start": 433.424,
    "end": 436.565,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "adhesive is placed between each layer,",
    "start": 436.625,
    "end": 438.446,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "then heat and pressure bond the stack.",
    "start": 438.766,
    "end": 440.506,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "Samsung and Micron have stayed with this",
    "start": 440.986,
    "end": 442.847,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "film-based family. SK Hynix used it too,",
    "start": 442.887,
    "end": 445.867,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "through the second generation of high",
    "start": 446.227,
    "end": 447.888,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "bandwidth memory. Then in 2019, SK Hynix",
    "start": 447.948,
    "end": 451.848,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "made a bet that would define the",
    "start": 451.908,
    "end": 453.349,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "next decade.",
    "start": 453.409,
    "end": 454.109,
    "scene": "scene_17"
  },
  {
    "text": "TC-NCF has a weakness that becomes serious",
    "start": 454.55,
    "end": 457.092,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "as stacks get taller. The film is",
    "start": 457.272,
    "end": 459.313,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "applied one layer at a time, and",
    "start": 459.373,
    "end": 461.114,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "each layer must be pressed and cured.",
    "start": 461.175,
    "end": 462.936,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "Trapped air can leave voids. The pressure",
    "start": 463.336,
    "end": 465.497,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "needed to bond thin dyes can cause",
    "start": 465.537,
    "end": 467.439,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "warpage, and the film sits between the",
    "start": 467.479,
    "end": 469.56,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "silicon and the heat spreader, adding",
    "start": 469.58,
    "end": 471.601,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "thermal resistance where heat needs to",
    "start": 471.661,
    "end": 473.643,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "escape. At eight layers, the process is",
    "start": 473.703,
    "end": 476.445,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "difficult. At 12, it becomes a yield",
    "start": 476.505,
    "end": 479.446,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "problem.",
    "start": 479.507,
    "end": 479.907,
    "scene": "scene_18"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix's alternative is called mass",
    "start": 480.368,
    "end": 482.79,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "reflow molded underfill or MR-MUF. Instead",
    "start": 482.89,
    "end": 486.552,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "of a film between every layer, the",
    "start": 486.572,
    "end": 488.353,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "entire stack is reflowed at once and",
    "start": 488.413,
    "end": 490.574,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "filled with a liquid epoxy molding",
    "start": 490.634,
    "end": 492.275,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "compound. The epoxy flows into the gaps",
    "start": 492.335,
    "end": 494.796,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "between the dyes and around the bumps,",
    "start": 494.857,
    "end": 496.397,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "then hardens. Because the material fills",
    "start": 496.658,
    "end": 498.979,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "the whole stack, it conducts heat better",
    "start": 499.019,
    "end": 501.14,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "and spreads stress more evenly.",
    "start": 501.5,
    "end": 504.062,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix also added up to four times",
    "start": 504.102,
    "end": 506.283,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "more thermal dummy bumps.",
    "start": 506.343,
    "end": 507.584,
    "scene": "scene_19"
  },
  {
    "text": "The results were measurable. SK Hynix",
    "start": 508.005,
    "end": 510.386,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "says its first MR-MUF process improved",
    "start": 510.426,
    "end": 513.226,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "heat dissipation by 36%. For 12 high",
    "start": 513.286,
    "end": 516.427,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "HBM3, it developed advanced MR-MUF with a",
    "start": 516.627,
    "end": 520.208,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "new molding compound offering 1.6 times",
    "start": 520.248,
    "end": 522.848,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "the heat dissipation. The process also",
    "start": 522.888,
    "end": 525.189,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "gave better warpage control and reduced",
    "start": 525.229,
    "end": 527.469,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "pressure on each die. By HBM3E mass",
    "start": 527.549,
    "end": 530.87,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "production, SK Hynix was reporting yields",
    "start": 530.91,
    "end": 533.971,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "around 70%.",
    "start": 534.031,
    "end": 534.511,
    "scene": "scene_20"
  },
  {
    "text": "That yield number is the heart of",
    "start": 534.952,
    "end": 536.293,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "the story. A memory stack is useless",
    "start": 536.333,
    "end": 538.633,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "if only half the finished units work.",
    "start": 538.813,
    "end": 540.474,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "NVIDIA needs millions of stacks on",
    "start": 540.994,
    "end": 542.955,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "schedule with reliability that survives",
    "start": 543.035,
    "end": 545.255,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "years in a data center. SK Hynix",
    "start": 545.295,
    "end": 547.636,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "could deliver them at volume. Samsung,",
    "start": 547.676,
    "end": 549.877,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "using its film-based process, struggled",
    "start": 550.157,
    "end": 552.378,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "with heat and yield on early HBM3E.",
    "start": 552.398,
    "end": 554.759,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "The result was not a permanent monopoly,",
    "start": 555.299,
    "end": 557.199,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "but it was close.",
    "start": 557.579,
    "end": 558.34,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "NVIDIA gave the largest share to the",
    "start": 559.0,
    "end": 560.781,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "supplier that could ship.",
    "start": 560.821,
    "end": 561.941,
    "scene": "scene_21"
  },
  {
    "text": "The irony is that SK Hynix nearly",
    "start": 562.382,
    "end": 564.504,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "went bankrupt before the boom. In 2023,",
    "start": 564.544,
    "end": 567.106,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "the memory market collapsed. Prices fell,",
    "start": 567.166,
    "end": 570.208,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "inventories piled up, and the company",
    "start": 570.528,
    "end": 572.63,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "reported an operating loss of more than",
    "start": 572.67,
    "end": 574.911,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "7.7 trillion Korean one. It was the",
    "start": 574.991,
    "end": 578.013,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "kind of year that forces a memory",
    "start": 578.053,
    "end": 579.975,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "maker to cut investment and retreat.",
    "start": 580.015,
    "end": 582.917,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix did the opposite. It kept betting",
    "start": 582.957,
    "end": 585.359,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "on high bandwidth memory and advanced",
    "start": 585.459,
    "end": 587.7,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "packaging.",
    "start": 587.78,
    "end": 588.241,
    "scene": "scene_22"
  },
  {
    "text": "The bet paid off faster than expected.",
    "start": 588.662,
    "end": 590.624,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "In 2024, SK Hynix reported an operating",
    "start": 591.144,
    "end": 594.367,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "profit of 23.5 trillion one. In 2025,",
    "start": 594.427,
    "end": 598.531,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "profit nearly doubled to 47.2 trillion one",
    "start": 598.911,
    "end": 601.974,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "on revenue of 97 trillion one. High",
    "start": 602.394,
    "end": 605.116,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "bandwidth memory grew into more than 40%",
    "start": 605.156,
    "end": 607.879,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "of its DRAM revenue. A business written",
    "start": 607.899,
    "end": 610.401,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "off as a commodity cyclical became the",
    "start": 610.481,
    "end": 612.923,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "most profitable supplier in the AI supply",
    "start": 612.963,
    "end": 615.605,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "chain.",
    "start": 615.665,
    "end": 615.966,
    "scene": "scene_23"
  },
  {
    "text": "High bandwidth memory is also a different",
    "start": 616.407,
    "end": 618.308,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "business from ordinary DRAM. It consumes",
    "start": 618.348,
    "end": 620.888,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "at least twice the wafer capacity of",
    "start": 620.949,
    "end": 622.629,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "standard memory for the same output",
    "start": 622.689,
    "end": 624.49,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "because of stacking and packaging. Every",
    "start": 624.87,
    "end": 626.99,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "bit of high bandwidth memory displaces two",
    "start": 627.03,
    "end": 629.091,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "bits of commodity DRAM. When demand",
    "start": 629.131,
    "end": 631.272,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "surges, supply cannot respond quickly.",
    "start": 631.332,
    "end": 633.732,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "Fabs take years to build and packaging",
    "start": 634.213,
    "end": 636.513,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "lines take months to qualify. The result",
    "start": 636.553,
    "end": 639.174,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "is pricing power that commodity memory",
    "start": 639.294,
    "end": 641.375,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "never enjoyed and a shortage that shows",
    "start": 641.435,
    "end": 643.776,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "up downstream.",
    "start": 643.856,
    "end": 644.656,
    "scene": "scene_24"
  },
  {
    "text": "Geography amplifies the concentration.",
    "start": 645.097,
    "end": 648.018,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix produces DRAM in Icheon and Cheongju,",
    "start": 648.058,
    "end": 650.64,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "South Korea. Its newest Fab M15X in",
    "start": 650.76,
    "end": 654.001,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "Chengdu represents an investment of more",
    "start": 654.041,
    "end": 656.142,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "than 20 trillion won and is designed",
    "start": 656.182,
    "end": 658.143,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "to ramp high bandwidth memory. A much",
    "start": 658.183,
    "end": 660.344,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "larger cluster is rising in Yangon with",
    "start": 660.404,
    "end": 662.745,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "a first Fab targeted for 2027. Advanced",
    "start": 662.785,
    "end": 665.986,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "packaging lines are being added in Chengdu",
    "start": 666.066,
    "end": 668.347,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "and Indiana. A single disruption can move",
    "start": 668.447,
    "end": 671.489,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "the entire artificial intelligence",
    "start": 671.529,
    "end": 673.47,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "roadmap.",
    "start": 673.55,
    "end": 673.99,
    "scene": "scene_25"
  },
  {
    "text": "The second chokepoint is outside Korea.",
    "start": 674.411,
    "end": 676.612,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "The GPU and its memory stacks must",
    "start": 677.072,
    "end": 679.072,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "be assembled on a silicon interposer",
    "start": 679.112,
    "end": 680.892,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "through a process called chip on wafer",
    "start": 680.992,
    "end": 682.833,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "on substrate or CoWoS. That process",
    "start": 682.893,
    "end": 685.773,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "belongs to TSMC. Starting with HBM4, the",
    "start": 685.813,
    "end": 689.394,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "memory's base die is built on a",
    "start": 689.434,
    "end": 690.975,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "logic process, bringing TSMC deeper into",
    "start": 691.015,
    "end": 693.755,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "the chain. Nvidia can design the",
    "start": 693.795,
    "end": 695.936,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "accelerator, but cannot ship it without",
    "start": 695.996,
    "end": 698.196,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "Korean memory and Taiwanese packaging.",
    "start": 698.276,
    "end": 700.557,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "Every side is a bottleneck.",
    "start": 701.117,
    "end": 702.657,
    "scene": "scene_26"
  },
  {
    "text": "That is why monopoly needs a qualifier.",
    "start": 703.098,
    "end": 704.919,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix does not control all of",
    "start": 705.42,
    "end": 707.261,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "it. Trend force expects it to hold",
    "start": 707.341,
    "end": 709.342,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "more than half the market, and Nvidia's",
    "start": 709.402,
    "end": 711.403,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "first HBM4 allocation reportedly gave",
    "start": 711.463,
    "end": 714.685,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "SK Hynix the mid 50% range, Samsung the",
    "start": 714.725,
    "end": 717.407,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "mid 20% range, and micron around 20%.",
    "start": 717.447,
    "end": 720.649,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "That is not a textbook monopoly. It",
    "start": 721.13,
    "end": 723.431,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "is a chokehold. The largest customer",
    "start": 723.491,
    "end": 725.792,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "cannot diversify faster than its second",
    "start": 725.872,
    "end": 728.154,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "supplier can fix its yield.",
    "start": 728.194,
    "end": 729.755,
    "scene": "scene_27"
  },
  {
    "text": "Concentration cuts both ways. SK Hynix",
    "start": 730.196,
    "end": 733.157,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "depends on Nvidia for much of its",
    "start": 733.257,
    "end": 734.698,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "high bandwidth memory revenue, and Nvidia",
    "start": 734.738,
    "end": 737.079,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "depends on SK Hynix for much of",
    "start": 737.099,
    "end": 738.84,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "its memory supply. Samsung is spending",
    "start": 738.9,
    "end": 741.181,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "heavily to close the yield gap, and",
    "start": 741.241,
    "end": 743.122,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "by 2026, it reported HBM4 yields",
    "start": 743.142,
    "end": 746.323,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "near 80%.",
    "start": 746.383,
    "end": 746.823,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "China's CXMT is trying to enter, though",
    "start": 747.804,
    "end": 750.405,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "its yields remain far behind. The lead",
    "start": 750.445,
    "end": 752.946,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "is real but not permanent, and that",
    "start": 753.006,
    "end": 755.067,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "uncertainty is priced into every forecast.",
    "start": 755.127,
    "end": 757.428,
    "scene": "scene_28"
  },
  {
    "text": "Next generation is here. HBM4 doubles the",
    "start": 757.929,
    "end": 760.811,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "interface from 1,024 bits to 2048 bits.",
    "start": 760.831,
    "end": 764.874,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "It supports 16 stack dies, 36 gigabytes",
    "start": 765.434,
    "end": 768.436,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "at 12 high and 48 at 16",
    "start": 768.477,
    "end": 770.258,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "high, and delivers around two terabytes",
    "start": 770.298,
    "end": 772.399,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "per second per stack. SK Hynix completed",
    "start": 772.459,
    "end": 775.181,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "development first in 2025 and is ramping",
    "start": 775.241,
    "end": 778.223,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "production for Nvidia's Vera Ruben",
    "start": 778.263,
    "end": 780.165,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "platform, bandwidth doubles again, and so",
    "start": 780.225,
    "end": 783.327,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "does the packaging difficulty.",
    "start": 783.407,
    "end": 784.788,
    "scene": "scene_29"
  },
  {
    "text": "Beyond HBM4, the industry is preparing to",
    "start": 785.229,
    "end": 788.031,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "remove the solder bumps entirely. The",
    "start": 788.071,
    "end": 790.493,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "technique is called hybrid bonding. It",
    "start": 790.513,
    "end": 792.755,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "presses two surfaces together, so copper",
    "start": 792.795,
    "end": 794.957,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "pads fuse directly with no solder balls",
    "start": 795.017,
    "end": 797.479,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "at all. The pitch shrinks from around",
    "start": 797.539,
    "end": 799.42,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "20 microns to below 1 micron. That",
    "start": 799.56,
    "end": 801.982,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "means more connections per square",
    "start": 802.022,
    "end": 803.463,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "millimeter, shorter paths, less heat, and",
    "start": 803.523,
    "end": 806.185,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "the ability to stack 16 or more",
    "start": 806.205,
    "end": 808.207,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "dies. SK high-necks has validated 12 high",
    "start": 808.247,
    "end": 811.609,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "hybrid bonding.",
    "start": 811.649,
    "end": 812.45,
    "scene": "scene_30"
  },
  {
    "text": "But hybrid bonding is not a free",
    "start": 812.851,
    "end": 814.492,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "lunch. Copper expands when heated, and the",
    "start": 814.532,
    "end": 817.054,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "surfaces must be almost perfectly flat and",
    "start": 817.114,
    "end": 819.295,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "clean. A single particle can create a",
    "start": 819.355,
    "end": 821.636,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "void across an entire interface. The",
    "start": 821.676,
    "end": 823.878,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "equipment is expensive, the process is",
    "start": 823.938,
    "end": 826.079,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "slow, and the yield-learning curve is",
    "start": 826.139,
    "end": 828.06,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "steep. That is why the industry is",
    "start": 828.12,
    "end": 830.062,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "delaying the transition where it can. The",
    "start": 830.102,
    "end": 832.463,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "physical limit is no longer the",
    "start": 832.523,
    "end": 834.104,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "transistor. It is the wire, the bump,",
    "start": 834.144,
    "end": 836.706,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "the adhesive, and the heat.",
    "start": 837.006,
    "end": 838.587,
    "scene": "scene_31"
  },
  {
    "text": "The lesson of high bandwidth memory is",
    "start": 839.008,
    "end": 840.809,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "simple. The artificial intelligence boom",
    "start": 840.889,
    "end": 843.21,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "is usually told as a story about",
    "start": 843.33,
    "end": 844.95,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "compute. But the companies that control",
    "start": 845.01,
    "end": 847.231,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "the path between compute and data have",
    "start": 847.271,
    "end": 849.072,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "as much leverage. Invidia designs the",
    "start": 849.112,
    "end": 851.513,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "brain. SK Hinex builds the memory that",
    "start": 851.553,
    "end": 854.034,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "feeds it. TSMC packages the two together.",
    "start": 854.134,
    "end": 856.955,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "The next battle is advanced packaging,",
    "start": 857.375,
    "end": 859.236,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "where interposers, hybrid bonding, and",
    "start": 859.556,
    "end": 861.917,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "eventually silicon photonics decide how",
    "start": 861.977,
    "end": 864.298,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "fast data can move. That is where",
    "start": 864.378,
    "end": 866.539,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  },
  {
    "text": "we go next.",
    "start": 866.559,
    "end": 867.199,
    "scene": "scene_32"
  }
]